            "firstname": "Salman ",
            "hidden": false,
            "title": "Chief Executive Officer",
            "bio": "An entrepreneur and key change maker in Saudi Arabia's hospitality and tourism sector, Mr. Salman Gasim is the CEO of Swiss Hospitality Company, a leading tourism capital development organisation in Saudi Arabia.\n\nHe is a driving force behind the shift towards global standards in Saudi hospitality, leading several key hospitality development projects and commissions, both locally and internationally.\n\nMr. Gasim is also the CEO at the Saudi Tourism Training and Recruitment Institute, known as the STTAR Institute, a specialised capability and professional development centre that has contributed to some of the largest human capability development projects and qualified over 10,000 Saudi calibers over the years.\n\nHe is currently the Vice President of the Saudi Regional European Business Council at the Federation of Saudi Chambers. In this role, he represents the Saudi business community in several European countries and leads the development of investment and economic relations.\n\nIn line with Vision 2030, he is committed to developing a new generation of hospitality leaders who will promote the highest level of service in the industry and strengthen Saudi Arabia's position as an innovative destination for hospitality and tourism.\n\n",
