            "firstname": "Widad",
            "hidden": false,
            "title": "Senior Reporter",
            "bio": "Widad Taleb is a Senior Reporter at CNN Business Arabic. She is of Lebanese origin, and was born and raised in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia. With extensive educational background in economics, she has worked in media for over 7 years. \n\nHer current role with CNN mainly focuses on gathering reports, presenting shows revolving around global energy markets, and conducting interviews with business pioneers and state officials globally. \n\nWidad has attended large-scale events both in and out of Saudi Arabia where many global ministers and business pioneers assembled, during which she developed an extensive network of relations, and interviewed government officials and business pioneers. She has also moderated sessions at large scale conferences in Saudi Arabia, such as Saudi Tadawul Group’s Saudi Capital Market Forum. \n\nWhen she reported on the Lebanese crisis from Beirut, Widad was also a regular commentator on live broadcasting stations, with appearances on various channels such as Sky News, RT, and Euro News.  \n\nWidad also volunteers some of her free time in the humanitarian field, whereby she has worked closely with several international organizations such as UN Women in promoting women empowerment, the UNHCR in providing refugee aid, in addition to being on the emergency response team following the large Beirut port blast.\n",
            "id": 3005892
