            "firstname": "Joseph",
            "hidden": false,
            "title": "Corporate Vice President - Human Resources",
            "bio": "With over 25 years of experience in the hospitality industry spanning the Middle East, Africa, and North America, Joseph Abou Yaghi is a seasoned Human Resources professional. He currently serves as the Corporate Vice President of Human Resources for Rotana, where he is responsible for overseeing the evaluation, creation, implementation, and maintenance of the company's Human Resources function. In his role, Joseph works closely with senior management to identify, coordinate, and manage HR services from Talent acquisition to Employee Development and Retention, Workforce Management, Compliance, Diversity and Inclusion, Compensation and Benefits, and other Human Resources Areas.\n\nJoseph's career at Rotana began in 2002 as a Director of Human Resources. During this time, he restructured the Human Resources organization at hotels and corporate levels, built and developed a team at the corporate office to support the company's fast development plans, and led a company cultural change by launching and implementing the new Rotana’s Core Competencies framework, which became the foundation for any future Human Resources initiative. He has also achieved notable accomplishments during his time at Rotana, including introducing development programmes such as DUROOB for Nationals and LEAD for General Managers, Executive Assistant Managers, and Potential Department Heads, and revamping and relaunching the Rotana Management Trainee program (TAROT).\n\nWith Rotana, Joseph is playing an integral part of the company stepping into new destinations like Jordan, Kinshasa, Iraq, Morocco, Turkey, Tanzania, Saudi Arabia, Bahrain and Qatar where he overlooked the opening of more than 30 properties. Prior to joining Rotana Hotels, Joseph worked for Marriott International and InterContinental Hotels Group in North America and the Middle East. \n\n\n\n\n",
