            "lastname": "Mahendra",
            "firstname": "Panchali",
            "hidden": false,
            "title": "President",
            "bio": "An industry power house Panchali Mahendra has over 6 years as the President of Atelier House Hospitality and experience in restaurant consulting and operations with 20 years of demonstrated history of working in the food & beverage industry along with 11 years in the Middle East. Skilled in Concepts, Feasibility, Food & Beverage, Business Planning, Operations Management, and Turnkey. With a strong consulting professional background with a PostGraduation focused on Guest Services Management from The Oberoi Center of Learning & Development and a Gold Medalist in Hospitality from the University of Huddersfield, UK & IHM Aurangabad.\n\nMahendra won her first 1 Michelin star as a restaurateur for her home-grown restaurant 11 woodfire in Dubai in June 2022. Her restaurant. 11, also made it to the World’s 50 best MENA at no.35 in Jan 2023. One of the only women restaurateurs to receive the Michelin award in Dubai, she is also the second Indian woman to be accredited with this world-renowned honor. Mahendra was also the first woman to receive Golden Visa in hospitality by the UAE government. Mahendra has also featured in Power 50 in 2020 and 2021, 2022 and Power women list four, 2020, 2021, 2022 and 2023 and been nominated for multiple awards across various channels and listed in multiple leaders and achieverslist including Caterer, CEO magazine, Entrepreneur magazine, CMO Asia, Hotel & Catering. Mahendra, recently was also awarded the heavy weight and made it to the TOP 30 All Star list. She has conceptualized, operated, and opened close to 70 restaurants internationally which is one of the highest ever done with significant success rate. Restaurants under her umbrella include – Marea, 11 woodfire, Mohalla, The Host, Tides Bar, RSVP in Dubai and Mohalla and Morini in KSA. She is also working on 4 major projects for 2023 opening. Mahendra, expanded into the India market and has opened the first ever Indian Japanese concept, INJA which is already one of the most talked about opening in the city.\n",
