            "lastname": "Morrow",
            "firstname": "Andrew",
            "hidden": false,
            "title": "Founder/Consultant ",
            "bio": "The founder of Tomorrow Hospitality, Andrew Morrow is a globally experienced hospitality specialist with proven experience in all facets of business operations from market research and financial planning through to concept development, operational set up and more. A recognized chef with over eighteen years’ experience in the kitchen, and a further twelve in operations and concept development across Australia, Canada, Europe, and the Middle East Andrew brings a wealth of knowledge, experience, and confidence to any project.\n\nEntering the middle east Market in 2007 during the growth phase of the region Andrew has seen the region come to life and is deeply rooted in the Middle east’s hospitality industry having worked the Global Restaurant Investment Forum as an advisory board member and guest speaker.\n\nIn previous roles with Roya international Andrew was a strategic advisor to multiple regional projects such as Place Vendome in Doha, Zabeel House and 25 Hours Hotel in Dubai, House Hotel Jeddah and many more. Andrew has also developed, launched, and operated brands such as Asia De Cuba Abu Dhabi, Leopold’s of London, Totora DIFC and Laluz DIFC.\n\nWithin the scope of brand acquisition Andrew has managed the negotiations for and successfully launched brands in the region including LARTE in Abu Dhabi and Dubai, Illy Caffe, Duoband and Andina, as well as managing the complete operator selection for multiple hotel projects including brand acquisition, franchise negotiations and operator agreements.\n\nAndrew brings passion and creativity to all his clients projects and works hard toward achieving financial and brand success on each project with the aim of ensuring long term successful growth.\n",
            "id": 3029191
